message: "If you use orchid in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ORCHID: Organic Rate-based CHarge-hopping and Integrated Device simulator"
abstract: >-
  ORCHID simulates charge and exciton transport in disordered organic semiconductors across
  scales: hopping rates (Miller-Abrahams, Marcus, Marcus-Levich-Jortner, Forster, Dexter),
  kinetic Monte Carlo and master-equation solvers, extended Gaussian disorder mobility laws,
  and drift-diffusion device models for OLEDs, organic solar cells and single-carrier diodes,
  with transfer-matrix optics. Device KMC couples charges and excitons with quenching and
  annihilation, and every module is validated against analytical limits or published results.
